{"step_index":151,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-06T17:00:31Z","content":"I see the issue! The screenshot you shared is from your live **web application** (DevOps QVS running on Spring Boot at `http://localhost:8080`), where the top navigation header bar was still displaying its default white background due to browser stylesheet caching and compiled `target/classes`.\n\n### What Was Done:\n1. **Sky Blue Background Applied to Navbar & Header**:\n   - Updated `.navbar` in [`style.css`](file:///C:/Users/Madziva/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/qualification-verification-system/src/main/resources/static/css/style.css#L58-L66) with:\n     ```css\n     .navbar {\n         background: #87CEEB !important; /* Vibrant Sky Blue */\n         backdrop-filter: blur(12px);\n         position: sticky;\n         top: 0;\n         z-index: 100;\n         border-bottom: 2px solid #5fa8cf;\n         box-shadow: 0 2px 10px rgba(14, 116, 144, 0.2);\n     }\n     ```\n2. **Enhanced Typography Contrast**:\n   - Adjusted brand title, subtitle, navigation links, and the `User: admin (ADMIN)` status to deep navy (`#0c4a6e` / `#0369a1`) so all text is crisp and readable on the sky blue background.\n3. **Hero & Announcement Styling**:\n   - Matched the top announcement bar and the hero header (`.hero-section`) with complementary light sky blue gradients (`#e0f2fe`).\n4. **Cache Invalidation & Hot Sync**:\n   - Added cache busters (`/css/style.css?v=skyblue`) to all templates (`index.html`, `dashboard.html`, `login.html`, `audit.html`).\n   - Synced the updated CSS directly into the active running server's `target/classes/`.\n\n---\n\n### How to See It in Your Browser:\nBecause browsers heavily cache stylesheets, please do a **Hard Refresh** on your page (`http://localhost:8080`):\n- Press **`Ctrl + F5`** (or **`Ctrl + Shift + R`**) in Chrome / Edge.\n\nThe header and navbar will now display with the sky blue background.","thinking":"**Updating UI with New Color Scheme**\n\nThe CSS file now includes a vibrant sky-blue navbar background with blur effect and subtle shadow. The announcement header uses a pale blue color. The hero section header has a linear gradient background.\n\n\n"}
